---
import { url } from '../../url';
import Doc from '../../layouts/Doc.astro';
import { company, email, product } from '../../site';
---

<Doc
  title="Wallyt terms of use"
  eyebrow="Wallyt"
  eyebrowHref="/wallyt"
  updated="2026-10-04"
  product={product('wallyt')}
  description="The terms for using Wallyt, the app for splitting shared costs, in plain language."
>
  <p>
    These terms are an agreement between you and {company.legalName}, whose product studio
    {company.brand} makes Wallyt (“we”, “us”). They apply to the Wallyt app and Wallyt on the web.
    By using Wallyt you agree to them. The <a href={url('/wallyt/privacy')}>privacy policy</a> explains
    what we do with your information.
  </p>

  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      <strong>In short:</strong> Wallyt is free. It keeps a shared record of who owes whom, but it
      doesn’t move money and it isn’t financial advice. Use it honestly, respect the people in your
      groups, and you can leave whenever you like.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Your account</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You need to be at least 13 years old, or older where the law of your country requires it.</li>
    <li>
      Use an email address that’s yours. Anyone who can read that inbox can sign in as you, so keep it
      secure.
    </li>
    <li>You’re responsible for what happens in Wallyt under your account.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Groups are shared</h2>
  <p>
    A group is a shared record. Everyone in it can see its expenses, payments, notes and history, and
    can add or change expenses. Its owner and admins can also add and remove people. Only share a
    group’s invite link with people you want in it.
  </p>
  <p>
    When you add someone to a group, by name or from your contacts, only add people you actually
    share costs with, and only use details they’d expect you to share with the group.
  </p>

  <h2>Wallyt doesn’t move money</h2>
  <p>
    Wallyt records what people say they spent and owe. It doesn’t hold, send or receive money, and
    we’re not part of any debt or payment between the people in a group. Balances are only as right as
    the expenses entered, so check them before you pay. Exchange rates come from public sources and
    can differ from the rate your bank or card gave you. Nothing in Wallyt is financial, tax or legal
    advice.
  </p>

  <h2>Use it fairly</h2>
  <p>Don’t use Wallyt to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>break the law, or help anyone else to;</li>
    <li>harass, threaten or impersonate anyone, or post content that does;</li>
    <li>add people or their details to a group without a good reason to;</li>
    <li>
      try to get into groups or accounts that aren’t yours, guess invite links, or test, disrupt or
      overload our servers;
    </li>
    <li>copy, scrape or resell Wallyt or its data, or build a competing service from it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What you add stays yours</h2>
  <p>
    You own the expenses, notes, names and photos you add. You let us store them, process them and show
    them to the people in your groups, only so that Wallyt can work. You can export a group’s expenses
    at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to Wallyt</h2>
  <p>
    Wallyt is free. We keep improving it, which means features can change or be removed. If we ever
    decide to close Wallyt, we’ll tell you ahead of time, by email or in the app, so you can export
    your groups first.
  </p>

  <h2>Ending your use</h2>
  <p>
    You can stop using Wallyt at any time, and <a href={url('/wallyt/delete-account')}>delete your account</a> whenever you like. We may suspend or close an account that breaks these terms or puts
    other people at risk. If we do, we’ll tell you why unless the law or someone’s safety stops us.
  </p>

  <h2>No guarantees</h2>
  <p>
    We work hard to keep Wallyt accurate and available, but it’s provided as it is, without promises
    that it will always be available, free of mistakes, or right for your purposes. As far as the law
    allows, {company.legalName} isn’t liable for indirect or consequential losses, or for money owed
    between the people in a group. Nothing in these terms limits rights you have under the law that
    can’t be limited by agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    If we change these terms, we’ll update the date at the top. If a change matters, we’ll let you know
    by email or in Wallyt before it takes effect. Using Wallyt after that means you accept the new
    terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    {company.brand}, the product studio of {company.legalName}<br />
    <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>
  </p>
</Doc>
